+# smallpt — The Light Lab
+
+Kevin Beason's C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly and rendered locally in a Web Worker. The original reflection, refraction, diffuse scattering, camera and Cornell box are preserved. The adapter adds progressive sample accumulation, an RGBA buffer and configurable colors for the mirror and glass spheres.
+
+## Run
+
+`pnpm start` serves the app on port 11222 (or `$PORT`). The compiled JavaScript and WebAssembly are included in `public/`; no compiler is needed to run the app. Serve over HTTP rather than opening index.html as a file.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+Install Emscripten and put `emcc` on your PATH, then run `pnpm build`. Built with Emscripten 6.0.1.
+
+`node scripts/check.cjs` checks pixel output, repeatability, randomized colors and seeds directly against the compiled WebAssembly, without a browser.
+
+`node scripts/preview.cjs` regenerates the 128-sample loading preview using the same WebAssembly renderer.
+
+Rendering starts automatically at 640 × 480. Quality selects the sample target and restarts rendering. Randomize & render chooses new sphere tints and a fresh seed; PNG export saves the current canvas. The worker keeps the interface responsive during rendering.
+
+Original source: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/ — Kevin Beason, MIT license, retained in `src/LICENSE.txt`. The unmodified upstream source is `src/smallpt-original.cpp`; the browser adapter is `src/renderer.cpp`.
